Touch ID passkeys saved by Effie itself (Chromium's own platform authenticator), macOS only.

Chromium keeps them in the keychain access group MAC_TEAM_ID.MAC_BUNDLE_ID.webauthn
(chrome_web_authentication_delegate.cc) and offers Touch ID only when the main executable is
signed with exactly that group (device/fido/mac/touch_id_context.mm). Chromium's branding leaves
the team empty, so it is never offered in CEF. With Effie's team and bundle ID the group is
Y3MJK95HD8.app.cierge.browser.webauthn, which spikes/signing/alter-passkeys.entitlements grants
(spikes/release.sh, with a Developer ID provisioning profile). The other keychain groups built from
these values (device-bound sessions, payments, device trust) move to Effie's team too; they were
unusable with an empty team before and stay off unless signed for.

--- a/chrome/app/theme/chromium/BRANDING
+++ b/chrome/app/theme/chromium/BRANDING
@@ -5,6 +5,6 @@
 PRODUCT_INSTALLER_FULLNAME=Chromium Installer
 PRODUCT_INSTALLER_SHORTNAME=Chromium Installer
 COPYRIGHT=Copyright @LASTCHANGE_YEAR@ The Chromium Authors. All rights reserved.
-MAC_BUNDLE_ID=org.chromium.Chromium
+MAC_BUNDLE_ID=app.cierge.browser
 MAC_CREATOR_CODE=Cr24
-MAC_TEAM_ID=
+MAC_TEAM_ID=Y3MJK95HD8
